<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The Maven module of the backend (feat-6-contracts-openapi-pipeline, Tasks 105.100 and 120.100).

  This module has no product code. It has the Spring server interfaces that the plugin openapi-generator-maven-plugin
  makes from contracts/openapi.yaml, and the libraries that this generated code needs to compile. Build with ./mvnw:
  the Maven Wrapper (.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties) pins the Maven version of tools/versions.env.

  The plugin has two executions (see the <build> section):
    - spring-interfaces, bound to the phase generate-sources. It writes the Java code to src/generated/java, and
      adds this folder as a compile source root (the plugin option addCompileSourceRoot, so no other plugin).
      `just generate` deletes the folder first and makes the code again. The folder is committed to git.
    - api-docs, bound to no phase (the HTML documentation, REQ-015). `just api-docs` starts it. It writes to
      build/api-docs (the folder is not in git).
  `just generate`, `just compile` and `just api-docs` compare the sha256 of the plugin jar with the pin
  OPENAPI_GENERATOR_MAVEN_PLUGIN_SHA256 of tools/versions.env before they start Maven (tools/gates/_lib.sh,
  verify_generator_plugin). The version of the plugin in this file and the version in tools/versions.env must
  be the same: `just check-pins` checks it.

   The libraries (the license of each one is in the plan of feat-6-contracts-openapi-pipeline):
      - NO bill of materials (BOM) is imported. A BOM can bring jakarta.annotation-api in again (EPL-2.0 OR GPL-2.0
        with Classpath-exception), and the owner decided on 2026-11-04 to use org.apache.tomcat:tomcat-annotations-api
        for jakarta.annotation.Generated. The Spring Boot BOM manages that artifact at 10.1.55, so the version of
        the artifact is named here (10.1.61). The scope of the artifact is provided (the annotation has SOURCE
        retention), so it stays off the runtime class path. `./mvnw dependency:tree` must not show jakarta.annotation-api.
     - The generator options annotationLibrary=none, documentationProvider=none and openApiNullable=false remove
       swagger-annotations-jakarta and jackson-databind-nullable. The generated code does not need them.

   The test tools (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 110, Tasks 110.100 and 110.130). The module has no
   product code, so the tests exercise the generated code (the example module). The license of each tool is in the
   license table of the plan; the two tools of the class Review (JUnit and jqwik, both EPL-2.0) have the deviation
   DEC 93a6d588-e002-4daf-9a47-45e2d77786e9 (the register of the approved deviations, accepted 2026-11-09). Every
   test tool is in <scope>test</scope>, so the cyclonedx plugin (includeTestScope, the default false) keeps them out
   of the SBOM: the licenses that the SBOM gate checks are the ones of the main dependencies above.
     - JUnit (org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter): the unit tests. The version is the one of tools/versions.env
       (JUNIT_VERSION). The 5.x line and not the 6.x line: jqwik 1.10.2 needs the JUnit Platform 1.14.x, and the
       engines of the two lines do not mix (the plan records the decision).
     - Testcontainers (org.testcontainers:testcontainers and the module org.testcontainers:postgresql,
       org.testcontainers:junit-jupiter): the integration tests (one lightweight container, postgres:16-alpine, the
       PostgreSQL license; the driver org.postgresql:postgresql is BSD-2-Clause). The version is the one of
       tools/versions.env (TESTCONTAINERS_VERSION, POSTGRESQL_VERSION). The 1.21.x line and not the 2.x core: the
       junit-jupiter module has no 2.x release, and the core and the modules must be the same line (the plan records
       the decision).
     - jqwik (net.jqwik:jqwik, EPL-2.0, the deviation DEC above): the property tests. The version is the one of
       tools/versions.env (JQWIK_VERSION).
      - maven-surefire-plugin (the version in tools/versions.env, MAVEN_SUREFIRE_PLUGIN_VERSION): runs the tests of
        the JUnit Platform (the JUnit engine and the jqwik engine).
      - PIT (org.pitest:pitest-maven, the build plugin, and org.pitest:pitest-junit5-plugin, the JUnit5 support of
        PIT as a dependency of the plugin): the mutation tests (the recipe mutation-backend). The versions are the
        ones of tools/versions.env (PIT_VERSION, PIT_JUNIT5_PLUGIN_VERSION). The configuration restricts the run to
        the generated model code (targetClasses) and to the unit tests of the generated code (targetTests, the class
        that is not successful and the integration test are no target tests), and it makes the HTML and the XML
        report in target/pit-reports (the folder is in .gitignore through target/). The plugin has no execution
        bound to a phase: the recipe starts the goal mutationCoverage after the phase test-compile in one run of
        ./mvnw (the generator execution of the phase generate-sources adds src/generated/java as a compile source
        root; without the phase, the project has no compile source root, and the goal skips).
       - JaCoCo (org.jacoco:jacoco-maven-plugin, the build plugin, EPL-2.0, the deviation DEC above): the coverage
        of the module (the recipe coverage-backend). The version is the one of tools/versions.env (JACOCO_VERSION).
        The plugin has no execution bound to a phase: the recipe starts the goals prepare-agent, the phase test
        (the unit tests, the normal run of surefire) and report in one run of ./mvnw, as for the mutation tool
        pitest-maven. prepare-agent sets the project property argLine, and the test runner maven-surefire-plugin
        (that has no own argLine) passes it to the forked JVM. The report (HTML and XML) is in target/site/jacoco
        (the folder is in .gitignore through target/). The configuration has no check goal and no rule: the recipe
        makes a report and no threshold is set (REQ-006, the walking skeleton sets the threshold from the
        measured baseline).

    The architecture tools (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 130, Tasks 130.100 and 130.120; DEC
    9edc1071-4fd0-48b6-a037-1a4cb2331f73). Every one is in <scope>test</scope>, so the cyclonedx plugin keeps it
    out of the SBOM, as for the test tools above. The versions are the ones of tools/versions.env (SPRING_MODULITH_VERSION,
    ARCHUNIT_VERSION and STRUCTURIZR_VERSION; just check-pins compares them, check_pins.py: check_maven_test_pins).
      - Spring Modulith (org.springframework.modulith:spring-modulith-core): the module structure of the module
        (R1, the recipe architecture-backend). The 1.4.x line and not the 2.x line: the core of the 2.x line (2.1.2,
        the last general-availability release) has the dependencies spring-core and spring-context 7.0.9, and the
        test support of the 2.x line (spring-modulith-test) has the Spring Boot 4 dependencies; the module has the
        Spring Framework 6.2.19 line and no Spring Boot (the plan records the decision). The core of 1.4.14 has the
        dependencies spring-core and spring-context 6.2.19, the same versions as the module, and it gives the
        module structure assertions (ApplicationModules.of(...), verify(), detectViolations()); the JUnit test
        starts them without a Spring context. The test support artifact of 1.4.14 (spring-modulith-test) is not in
        the module: its annotation @ApplicationModuleTest boots a Spring context (the annotation is wired to
        @SpringBootTest), and the module has no Spring Boot.
      - Spring Boot (org.springframework.boot:spring-boot, the scope test): a dependency of the code of Spring
        Modulith 1.4.14 that the POM of the artifact does not declare. The factory ApplicationModules.of(...) of
        the core starts the lookup of the detection strategy
        (org.springframework.modulith.core.ApplicationModuleDetectionStrategyLookup), and that lookup calls the
        method applyTo of the class ConfigDataEnvironmentPostProcessor of this artifact in each start (a start
        without the jar stops with the error NoClassDefFoundError). The version 3.5.16 is the one that the line
        1.4.x of Spring Modulith has as its optional dependency (the POM of the core names 3.5.16 for
        spring-boot-autoconfigure), and its dependencies are spring-core and spring-context 6.2.19, the same
        versions as the module (no other jar enters the test class path). The module has no class of Spring Boot,
        and no context of Spring Boot starts: the jar is in the scope test, and it stays out of the SBOM.
      - ArchUnit (com.tngtech.archunit:archunit and archunit-junit5): the layer rule of the module (R2, the recipe
        architecture-backend), and the source of the package dependencies of the comparison with the model (the
        recipe architecture-model). The core of Spring Modulith has the dependency archunit 1.4.2; the module names
        1.5.1, and the resolution of Maven gives 1.5.1 (the nearest dependency wins).
      - structurizr-client (com.structurizr:structurizr-client): the reader of the workspace of model/
        (com.structurizr.io.json.JsonReader, the model classes of structurizr-core). The module has no product code
        and no other reader of the workspace, so the client artifact (the JSON reader) and not the DSL artifact
        (structurizr-dsl, that has the client as a dependency and the parsers for the other formats) is in the
        module. The dependencies of the client (jackson-databind, httpclient5, jaxb-api and structurizr-core) are
        in the scope test too, and the cyclonedx plugin keeps them out of the SBOM.


    The test classes are in src/test/java/biz/dfch/specmgrdemo/testtools/ (the test tools of the phases 110 and
    120) and in src/test/java/biz/dfch/specmgrdemo/architecture/ (the architecture tools of the phase 130: the
    module structure R1, the layer rule R2 and the comparison with the model of the recipe architecture-model). A
    class whose name has no suffix `Test` (or `IT` for the integration tests) is a case that is not successful
    (ACC-002 of the plan): the default run of surefire does not start it, and the recipes run it separately and stop
    for it (tools/gates/test-*-*.sh and tools/gates/architecture-*.sh). The suffix IT keeps the integration tests
    out of the unit run.
 -->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <groupId>biz.dfch.specmgrdemo</groupId>
  <artifactId>backend</artifactId>
  <version>0.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <name>biz.dfch.SpecMgrDemo backend</name>
  <description>The Java backend. This module has no product code. It has the generated Spring server interfaces.</description>

  <licenses>
    <license>
      <name>GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 only</name>
      <url>https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt</url>
    </license>
  </licenses>

  <properties>
    <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
    <!-- The JDK of tools/versions.env (JDK_VERSION) is Temurin 21. -->
    <maven.compiler.release>21</maven.compiler.release>
    <!-- A fixed time stamp, so that the archives of a build are the same in each run. -->
    <project.build.outputTimestamp>2026-11-04T00:00:00Z</project.build.outputTimestamp>

    <!-- The generator. tools/versions.env has the same version (OPENAPI_GENERATOR_MAVEN_PLUGIN_VERSION). -->
    <openapi-generator.version>7.27.0</openapi-generator.version>
    <!-- The libraries that the generated code needs. Each version is named here, and no BOM gives one. -->
    <spring.version>6.2.19</spring.version>
    <jakarta-validation.version>3.0.2</jakarta-validation.version>
    <jackson-annotations.version>2.21</jackson-annotations.version>
    <tomcat-annotations-api.version>10.1.61</tomcat-annotations-api.version>
    <!-- The test tools (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 110). Each version is the one of
         tools/versions.env (just check-pins compares them). The scope of every test tool is test. -->
    <junit.version>5.14.4</junit.version>
    <testcontainers.version>1.21.4</testcontainers.version>
    <postgresql.version>42.7.14</postgresql.version>
    <jqwik.version>1.10.2</jqwik.version>
    <maven-surefire-plugin.version>3.6.1</maven-surefire-plugin.version>
    <!-- The mutation tests (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 120). Each version is the one of
         tools/versions.env (just check-pins compares them). -->
    <pitest.version>1.30.2</pitest.version>
    <pitest-junit5-plugin.version>1.2.3</pitest-junit5-plugin.version>
    <!-- The architecture tools (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 130). Each version is the one of
          tools/versions.env (just check-pins compares them). The scope of every architecture tool is test.
          Spring Modulith is the 1.4.x line and not the 2.x line (the 2.x line needs the Spring Framework 7 line,
          the module has 6.2.19; see the header comment). -->
    <spring-modulith.version>1.4.14</spring-modulith.version>
    <!-- The Spring Boot jar that the code of Spring Modulith 1.4.14 needs for the module detection (see the
         header comment). The 3.5.x line is the one of the Spring Framework 6.2.x line of the module. -->
    <spring-boot.version>3.5.16</spring-boot.version>
    <archunit.version>1.5.1</archunit.version>
    <structurizr.version>6.2.4</structurizr.version>
    <!-- The coverage (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 140). The version is the one of
         tools/versions.env (just check-pins compares it, check_pins.py: check_maven_test_pins). -->
    <jacoco.version>0.8.16</jacoco.version>

    <!-- The files that the generators read and write, relative to the folder of this module. -->
    <contract.file>${project.basedir}/../contracts/openapi.yaml</contract.file>
    <generated.java.dir>${project.basedir}/src/generated</generated.java.dir>
    <api-docs.dir>${project.basedir}/../build/api-docs</api-docs.dir>
  </properties>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- ResponseEntity and the annotations of Spring Web MVC (@RequestMapping, @RequestParam and others). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-web</artifactId>
      <version>${spring.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- @Validated of the generated interfaces. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-context</artifactId>
      <version>${spring.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- Jakarta Bean Validation, the API only (no implementation: the generated code needs none to compile). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>jakarta.validation</groupId>
      <artifactId>jakarta.validation-api</artifactId>
      <version>${jakarta-validation.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- @JsonProperty and @JsonValue of the generated model classes. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.fasterxml.jackson.core</groupId>
      <artifactId>jackson-annotations</artifactId>
      <version>${jackson-annotations.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- jakarta.annotation.Generated (Jakarta Annotations 2.1) in place of jakarta.annotation-api. Decision of the
          owner of 2026-11-04. The version is named here, and no BOM gives it. The scope is provided: the annotation
          has SOURCE retention (it is read at compile time only), so the jar stays off the runtime class path, and a
          later Spring Boot starter cannot bring jakarta.annotation-api in again with a duplicate class. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.tomcat</groupId>
      <artifactId>tomcat-annotations-api</artifactId>
      <version>${tomcat-annotations-api.version}</version>
      <scope>provided</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The test tools (the scope test keeps them out of the SBOM, see the header comment). -->
    <!-- JUnit 5 (EPL-2.0, the deviation DEC 93a6d588-e002-4daf-9a47-45e2d77786e9). The 5.x line: jqwik needs the
         JUnit Platform 1.14.x. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
      <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
      <version>${junit.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- Testcontainers (MIT): the core, the JUnit module and the PostgreSQL module, the 1.21.x line (see the header). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
      <artifactId>testcontainers</artifactId>
      <version>${testcontainers.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
      <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
      <version>${testcontainers.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
      <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
      <version>${testcontainers.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The JDBC driver of the container (BSD-2-Clause, test scope only: not in the SBOM). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.postgresql</groupId>
      <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
      <version>${postgresql.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- jqwik (EPL-2.0, the deviation DEC 93a6d588-e002-4daf-9a47-45e2d77786e9): the property tests. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>net.jqwik</groupId>
      <artifactId>jqwik</artifactId>
      <version>${jqwik.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The architecture tools (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 130; see the header comment). The
         scope test keeps them out of the SBOM. -->
    <!-- Spring Modulith (Apache-2.0): the module structure (R1). The 1.4.x line (the module has the Spring
         Framework 6.2.19 line; the 2.x line needs the 7 line, the plan records the decision). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.modulith</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-modulith-core</artifactId>
      <version>${spring-modulith.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The jar that the module detection of Spring Modulith 1.4.14 calls in each start (the class
         ConfigDataEnvironmentPostProcessor; see the header comment). Its dependencies are spring-core and
         spring-context 6.2.19, the versions of the module. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot</artifactId>
      <version>${spring-boot.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- ArchUnit (Apache-2.0, the bundled OW2 ASM is BSD-3-Clause): the layer rule (R2) and the package
         dependencies of the comparison with the model. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.tngtech.archunit</groupId>
      <artifactId>archunit</artifactId>
      <version>${archunit.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.tngtech.archunit</groupId>
      <artifactId>archunit-junit5</artifactId>
      <version>${archunit.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- structurizr-client (Apache-2.0): the reader of the workspace of model/ (the JSON reader and the model
         classes). The comparison test of the recipe architecture-model (Task 130.120). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.structurizr</groupId>
      <artifactId>structurizr-client</artifactId>
      <version>${structurizr.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <plugins>
      <!-- The test runner (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 110). The version is the one of
           tools/versions.env (MAVEN_SUREFIRE_PLUGIN_VERSION). The default includes of surefire (Test*, *Test,
           *Tests, *TestCase) keep the cases that are not successful (the classes without a suffix, see the header)
           out of the unit run. The tests of the JUnit Platform (the JUnit engine and the jqwik engine) are found
           without further configuration. -->
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${maven-surefire-plugin.version}</version>
      </plugin>
       <!-- The mutation tests (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 120, Task 120.100). No execution is
            bound to a phase: the recipe mutation-backend starts the goal after the phase test-compile in one run
            of ./mvnw (./mvnw test-compile org.pitest:pitest-maven:<PIT_VERSION>:mutationCoverage
            -Dcodegen.skip=true). The phase is necessary: the generator execution of the phase generate-sources
            adds src/generated/java as a compile source root, and the goal skips a project with no compile source
            root. PIT mutates the compiled classes of the module (target/classes, the generated code; the module
            has no product code) and runs the target tests on each mutant.
           The configuration keeps the run small and deterministic (the plan records it, Result of the Phase 120):
           - targetClasses: the generated model code only. The package biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.api has the interface
             StatusApi, and an interface has no bytecode with logic, so there is no mutant in it.
           - targetTests: the unit tests of the generated code only. The class that is not successful (no suffix
             Test) and the integration test (the suffix IT, it needs the Docker daemon) are no target tests.
            - outputFormats: the HTML report (the default folder target/pit-reports) and the XML report
              (mutations.xml, the deterministic source the recipe asserts on for the surviving mutants).
           The JUnit5 support of PIT (the JUnit engine of the JUnit Platform and the jqwik engine) is the plugin
           dependency pitest-junit5-plugin: pitest-maven loads the test framework plugins from its own classpath,
           and not from the test classpath of the module. -->
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.pitest</groupId>
        <artifactId>pitest-maven</artifactId>
        <version>${pitest.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <targetClasses>
            <param>biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.model.*</param>
          </targetClasses>
          <targetTests>
            <param>biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.testtools.ErrorCodeTest</param>
            <param>biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.testtools.ErrorCodePropertyTest</param>
          </targetTests>
          <outputFormats>
            <outputFormat>HTML</outputFormat>
            <outputFormat>XML</outputFormat>
          </outputFormats>
        </configuration>
        <dependencies>
          <dependency>
            <groupId>org.pitest</groupId>
            <artifactId>pitest-junit5-plugin</artifactId>
            <version>${pitest-junit5-plugin.version}</version>
          </dependency>
        </dependencies>
      </plugin>
       <!-- The coverage (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 140, Task 140.110). No execution is
            bound to a phase: the recipe coverage-backend starts the goals prepare-agent, the phase test and
            report in one run of ./mvnw (the same way as pitest-maven, see above). The goal prepare-agent sets
            the project property argLine before the phase test runs, and the test runner
            maven-surefire-plugin (that has no own argLine configuration) passes it to the forked JVM. The
            goal report reads the execution data (target/jacoco.exec) and makes the report in
            target/site/jacoco (the HTML report index.html and the XML report jacoco.xml, the parameter
            formats; the folder is in .gitignore through target/). The XML report is the deterministic
            source that the recipe asserts on (the counters of the report element). The configuration has
            no check goal and no rule: the recipe makes a report and no threshold is set (REQ-006). The
            version is the one of tools/versions.env (JACOCO_VERSION, just check-pins compares it). -->
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.jacoco</groupId>
        <artifactId>jacoco-maven-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${jacoco.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <formats>
            <format>XML</format>
            <format>HTML</format>
          </formats>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.openapitools</groupId>
        <artifactId>openapi-generator-maven-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${openapi-generator.version}</version>
        <executions>
          <!-- The Spring server interfaces (REQ-004). Options: the four of the task 090.120 (interfaceOnly,
               skipDefaultInterface, hideGenerationTimestamp and generateSupportingFiles), and the options that the
               agent set (see the plan, Decisions Made). -->
          <execution>
            <id>spring-interfaces</id>
            <phase>generate-sources</phase>
            <goals>
              <goal>generate</goal>
            </goals>
            <configuration>
              <inputSpec>${contract.file}</inputSpec>
              <generatorName>spring</generatorName>
              <output>${generated.java.dir}</output>
              <apiPackage>biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.api</apiPackage>
              <modelPackage>biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.model</modelPackage>
              <generateSupportingFiles>false</generateSupportingFiles>
              <generateApiTests>false</generateApiTests>
              <generateModelTests>false</generateModelTests>
              <generateApiDocumentation>false</generateApiDocumentation>
              <generateModelDocumentation>false</generateModelDocumentation>
              <addCompileSourceRoot>true</addCompileSourceRoot>
              <configOptions>
                <interfaceOnly>true</interfaceOnly>
                <skipDefaultInterface>true</skipDefaultInterface>
                <hideGenerationTimestamp>true</hideGenerationTimestamp>
                <useSpringBoot3>true</useSpringBoot3>
                <sourceFolder>java</sourceFolder>
                <annotationLibrary>none</annotationLibrary>
                <documentationProvider>none</documentationProvider>
                <openApiNullable>false</openApiNullable>
                <!-- Both are the defaults of 7.27.0. The generator writes a warning if they are not set. -->
                <generateJsonIncludeAnnotations>false</generateJsonIncludeAnnotations>
                <generateJsonSetterNullsAnnotations>false</generateJsonSetterNullsAnnotations>
              </configOptions>
            </configuration>
          </execution>
          <!-- The API documentation (REQ-015): the generator html2. No phase: `just api-docs` starts it with
               the goal openapi-generator:generate@api-docs. The output is not in git. -->
          <execution>
            <id>api-docs</id>
            <phase>none</phase>
            <goals>
              <goal>generate</goal>
            </goals>
            <configuration>
              <inputSpec>${contract.file}</inputSpec>
              <generatorName>html2</generatorName>
              <output>${api-docs.dir}</output>
              <addCompileSourceRoot>false</addCompileSourceRoot>
              <configOptions>
                <hideGenerationTimestamp>true</hideGenerationTimestamp>
              </configOptions>
            </configuration>
          </execution>
        </executions>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
